homelab-haproxy (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add send-proxy to every generated backend server line, confirmed
    against this project's own production HAProxy (proxy01), which
    uses exactly this on every mail-stack backend so postfix/dovecot
    see the real client IP instead of the proxy's own

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:59:51 -0500

homelab-haproxy (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: HAProxy TCP-passthrough edge for raw-TCP
    protocols (SMTP, submission, IMAP, IMAPS) -- decouples "holds the
    public IP" from "runs the actual service" so homelab-postfix/
    homelab-dovecot can move off the internet-facing host while their
    ports keep working from the same public IP. homelab-haproxy-apply-
    backends regenerates /etc/haproxy/haproxy.cfg wholesale from an
    editable backends.yml, validating with `haproxy -c` before ever
    touching the live config -- a failed validation leaves the
    previous working config completely untouched. Explicitly does not,
    and structurally cannot, handle DNS's UDP traffic; out of scope for
    this tool by design, not an oversight

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 12 Sep 2026 22:46:36 -0500
